W44-98 baseline-diff: production W44-98 vs forced-variant-Z baseline
====================================================================

Date: 2026-05-19
Workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-98-dct16x32-lift-z
Parent commit: 935ea9e1 (W44-97)
Bench file: w44_98_baseline_diff_2026-05-19.tsv
Reproducer:
  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
    --features '__expert butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel' \
    --example w44_98_baseline_diff

Purpose
-------

Direct A/B between:
  - production: the new W44-98 dispatch (m3 sub-discriminator routes
    1420710-class to high_colour table, 1531677-class to default
    variant Z)
  - baseline: forces `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed_z()` on every
    W44-96-gated cell, equivalent to origin/main behaviour before
    W44-98 landed

29 cells: 7 OPEN + 3 W95_REGR + 6 W93_REGR + 6 W96_FIXED + 7 SPOT_FIXED.

Aggregate
---------

  OPEN→FIXED closes:               3
  FIXED→OPEN regressions:          0
  Worst SSIM2 delta vs baseline:   -0.0275 (1420710 e7 d=5)
  Total byte delta:                -1741B over 29 cells

All 3 closes are on 1420710 (m3=32.93). All 1531677 cells (m3=12.30)
are byte-identical to baseline — production correctly leaves them on
the variant Z table. All W95_REGR and W93_REGR cells are byte-identical
(gate doesn't fire — different mask range or wrong feature class).

Acceptance gate verification
----------------------------

(a) ≥3 OPEN close: PASS (3)
(b) Zero FIXED→OPEN flips: PASS (0)
(c) SSIM2 regression ≤ 0.3 on any cell: PASS (worst -0.0275)
(d) W93_REGR (1189261 + 1418519) cells byte-identical: PASS (6/6)
(e) W95_REGR (2389166 + 3637739) cells byte-identical: PASS (3/3)
(f) SPOT_FIXED cells stay FIXED: PASS (all 7 byte-identical)
(g) W96_FIXED cells (W44-96 close cells) stay FIXED: PASS (4 improved
    on 1420710 by 125-273B with SSIM2 ±0.02; 2 1531677 cells unchanged)
